From bfb464638ced5e57a9ed166b086e16c7fd008782 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:35:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] blitz-dom: a <use> draws an element of another SVG resource
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`<use href="sprite.svg#icon">` drew nothing: Blitz collects only
same-document fragment references, and usvg loads no external `use`.
A `<use>` whose href names another resource now has it fetched through
the document's NetProvider, as an inline SVG's `<image>` is, and kept
by the resource's URL. When its `<svg>` is constructed, the element it
names, and what that element refers to in its resource (`href="#…"`,
`url(#…)`), is copied into the `<svg>`'s `<defs>` with prefixed ids, and
the `<use>` refers to the copy. It is drawn in the context of the
`<use>`, as a same-document `<use>` is, so `currentColor` is the use
site's. The resource arriving late, sent again, or the href changing
constructs the `<svg>` again.
---
 packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/construct.rs |   1 +
 packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs          |   4 +-
 packages/blitz-dom/src/svg_image.rs        | 277 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 272 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

